parts.numbers:
**Measured** (doc/BITACORA, results_*.txt, file sizes on disk)
- Block size on disk:
  - fast profile: 10.4 GB;
  - compact profile: 5.74 GB (256-bit codes, same quality) or 5.24 GB (192-bit, −1 %) (E29). The ~4.96 GB figure assumes format tweaks and is an estimate.
- Runtime models (file sizes, 0.38 GB in total):
  - embed int8 IR: 272.5 MB bin + 3.5 MB xml;
  - Gemma tokenizer: 32.2 MB;
  - lm-hn-70m.hnzlm: 71.7 MB;
  - LM tokenizer: 3.6 MB.
- Fast-profile latencies (E26, medians):
  - hot hybrid: 25.9 ms; keyword: 3.1 ms; listing: 4 ms;
  - cold fragments: 280/284 ms; full cold text for 10 results: 525 ms;
  - cache hits: L1 24 ms, L2 53 ms;
  - opening the archive: 180 ms (3 segments, 637k docs).
- Query embedding: int8 on CPU 19–24 ms; fp16 45 ms. CPU compile of the fp16 IR took 3.8 s (E14).
- LM:
  - decode ~2,300 tokens/s with 64 slots on 8 threads; full-record decode 29 records/s (verify);
  - compression 120–129 records/s on 16 threads;
  - mean record length 77.3 tokens (2024-01).
- LM oversubscription pathology: a 10-record batch took 17,304 ms with spin pool and rayon competing, vs 1,033 ms with the default 8 spin threads (E17).
- Document embedding:
  - iGPU fp16 with buckets: 204 docs/s overall (per bucket: 565 at s32, 163 at s128, 81 at s256);
  - iGPU drops to 126–131 docs/s while the CPU runs the LM;
  - CPU: 19.9 docs/s;
  - NPU: fails to compile.
- OpenVINO 2026.4.1 pip package: 247 MB installed. The minimal DLL set (openvino, openvino_c, intel_cpu, intel_gpu, ir_frontend, tbb12, tbbbind, tbbmalloc) is 98.9 MB for CPU+GPU (plus 8.8 MB `cache.json`), or 64.2 MB for CPU only.
- Authors per monthly segment: 10.6k (2010-06), 30.6k (2015-06), 46.1k (2024-01); 9–10 B per name.

**Computed** (from code and model shapes)
- LM KV cache: 24 KiB per token per sequence (6 layers × K,V × 512 × f32).
  - 128-token prefix: 3 MiB.
  - 2,000-token record (MAX_TOKENS): ~47 MiB.
  - Today's capacity doubling (K transposed buffers, V Vec growth) can allocate up to about 2×.
- Logits: 196 KiB per active row per step (vocab 50,304), so 12.3 MiB at 64 rows.
- Today's `decode_records_each` puts every requested record in one batch, so a 200-candidate rerank needs about 600 MiB of KV inside a single query.
- Resident small indexes for 49.3 M docs: flags 49.3 MB, lm.idx offsets 12.3 MB, vec.has 6.2 MB, meta.idx 0.8 MB.
- LM work per cold compact query: ~100 candidates × ~60–77 tokens ≈ 6–8k tokens ≈ 2.6–3.4 s of the shared ~2,300 tokens/s. Aggregate throughput is therefore about 0.3–0.4 cold compact queries/s whatever the concurrency.
- Per-query engine memory:
  - k=10: a few MB.
  - k=500 with type filters and ×16 retries over all segments in parallel: from about 0.1 GB to over 1 GB transient, worst case from the kc/c1 formulas. It must be reserved and capped at admission.

**Estimates** (to measure)
- Binary sizes: `_hnz.pyd` 5–8 MB; wheel 2–3 MB compressed.
- Python boundary: under 10 µs per call; dict-to-dataclass ~3–6 µs per hit; pythonize of 10 hits ~50 µs.
- Mandatory RAM:
  - compact, CPU only: ~0.75–1.1 GB. This includes:
    - LM: 72 MB;
    - LM tokenizer: 15–30 MB;
    - Gemma tokenizer: 80–200 MB;
    - OpenVINO CPU int8 compiled model: 300–450 MB;
    - flags and offsets: ~70 MB;
    - authors: 85–140 MB as `Vec<String>`, or 20–35 MB as blob plus offsets;
    - LM KV minimum (16 slots): 48 MB;
    - scratch: 50–100 MB.
  - GPU document embedder: +0.3–0.6 GB of shared iGPU memory, which is system RAM.
  - Practical minimum: `ram="2GB"` for compact with rerank; ~0.25–0.4 GB for keyword-only.
- `open()` time for all of HN: ~1–4 s on CPU only; +3–10 s for the GPU compile without an OpenVINO cache dir (a cache dir costs ~0.3 GB of disk).
- Canary self-test: 0.1–0.3 s.
- Compact query: p50 ~4 s when run alone (E27 panel estimate); ~6–12 s each with 2–4 cold queries concurrently.

